@startuml rank-regime-replay
' ============================================================================
' RankRegime replay drop-rule — the SAFETY-CRITICAL decision a recovering
' reader makes for EVERY WAL record, keyed on the file/segment's rank_regime
' (header byte 28) and whether the record carries a durable CommitRank.
' Source of truth:
'   src/persistent_artrie/core/wal/header.rs   (RankRegime { Owned=0, Overlay=1 })
'   src/persistent_artrie/core/recovery.rs     (reconcile_lww / generation_of /
'                                               the `RankRegime::Overlay => continue` drop)
'
' LAYOUT: a top regime decision followed by a VERTICAL STACK of the three
' disjoint outcome cases (condition -> action -> rationale, one colored card
' each), so the figure reads top-to-bottom within the prose column. The three
' cards partition every record: RANKED (kept), UNRANKED+Owned (kept), and
' UNRANKED+Overlay (dropped as a two-append orphan).
'
' Color key:  amber #FFE0B2 = control / regime decision (frontier)
'             green #C8E6C9 = KEEP — the record contributes to recovered state
'             red   #FFCDD2 = DROP — the record is a two-append orphan, discarded
'             grey  #ECEFF1 = terminal / infrastructure
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam wrapWidth 300
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #37474F
  FontName "DejaVu Sans"
}
skinparam card {
  BorderColor #37474F
  FontName "DejaVu Sans"
}

title RankRegime replay drop-rule\nper record: generation_of(lsn) = rank.unwrap_or(lsn)

card "recover()  ▶\nreplay the durable WAL" as START #ECEFF1

rectangle "read next durable WAL\nrecord (lsn, record)" as READ #ECEFF1

rectangle "**per record** — stamp\ngeneration_of(lsn) = rank.unwrap_or(lsn)\nclassify by: (durable **CommitRank**?,\nheader **rank_regime**). Three\ndisjoint outcomes ↓" as DECIDE #FFE0B2

card "**CASE 1 · RANKED → KEEP**\n--\n**when:** the record carries a\ndurable **CommitRank**\n**do:** KEEP — generation = its rank\n(the op committed: CAS won AND rank\nwas durably bound before the ack)\n**why:** ranked ⇒ KEPT for any\nregime. Stamp gen_of(lsn) = rank;\nreconcile per term by MAX(gen, lsn)\n⇒ LSN replay == CAS state." as C1 #C8E6C9

card "**CASE 2 · Owned → KEEP**\n--\n**when:** no CommitRank ∧ header\n**rank_regime = Owned (0)**\n**do:** KEEP in LSN order\n(generation = lsn)\n**why:** Owned / legacy / base /\nvocab — NO record is ranked, so each\nunranked record is a confirmed\nin-order append. gen = lsn ⇒\nstable replay." as C2 #C8E6C9

card "**CASE 3 · Overlay → DROP**\n--\n**when:** no CommitRank ∧ header\n**rank_regime = Overlay (1)**\n**do:** DROP — `continue` (skip the\nrecord): a **two-append orphan**\n**why:** Overlay — every CONFIRMED\nop carries a rank. An unranked\nrecord is the gap between the data\nappend and the (never-written) rank\n— a crash in the two-append window,\nso the op was NEVER acked. Keeping\nit RESURRECTS a write no caller saw\nsucceed. THE SAFETY-CRITICAL RULE." as C3 #FFCDD2

rectangle "emit the kept op (or nothing\nfor a dropped record) into the\n(generation, lsn) merge" as EMIT #ECEFF1

card "◼ recovered state =\nlast committed writer per term" as DONE #ECEFF1

START --> READ
READ --> DECIDE
DECIDE --> C1 : record carries a\ndurable **CommitRank**
C1 --> C2 : else · UNRANKED\n∧ regime = Owned (0)
C2 --> C3 : else · UNRANKED\n∧ regime = Overlay (1)
C3 --> EMIT
EMIT --> DONE

legend bottom
| Color | Outcome |
|<#FFE0B2>| regime decision |
|<#C8E6C9>| KEEP (recovered) |
|<#FFCDD2>| DROP (orphan) |
endlegend
@enduml
